WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:05.710
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.290
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.610 --> 00:15.410
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.410 --> 00:20.720
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.720 --> 00:25.290
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.890
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.890 --> 00:34.110
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.610
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.330 --> 02:17.070
<b>The 300-Limit Pandemonium</b>

02:11.410 --> 02:14.570
You beat the ninth already, did you?

02:15.520 --> 02:17.070
Guess it's perfect timing.

02:17.560 --> 02:18.800
Vash?

02:18.800 --> 02:21.490
Dadd—I mean, Boss!

02:21.490 --> 02:27.250
I thought I'd make your tenth 
opponent a monster I caught.

02:27.250 --> 02:29.490
I went on a bit of an excursion for it.

02:44.090 --> 02:48.030
A human? Yeah, don't think so...

02:48.790 --> 02:50.310
A sorcerer type?

02:50.600 --> 02:53.620
One of those dummies from 
long, long, long ago

02:54.020 --> 02:58.730
who tried to fuse with a 
tree to gain longer life.

03:00.160 --> 03:03.890
I doubt you can beat him 
in the state you're in now,

03:03.890 --> 03:06.840
so I'll pick a different win criteria.

03:07.910 --> 03:09.330
What's that?

03:09.330 --> 03:11.680
Survive five minutes.

03:11.270 --> 03:24.090
Unique Scenario
 <b>Invitation From Rabituza
Practical Training  Opponent 10
Aberrant Woodmage</b>

03:11.680 --> 03:15.210
<i>Unique Scenario.
"Invitation From Rabituza."</i>

03:15.690 --> 03:18.030
<i>Practical training, opponent 10:</i>

03:18.030 --> 03:19.340
<i>Aberrant Woodmage.</i>

03:19.780 --> 03:24.090
Clear Condition
 <b>Survive for five minutes</b>

03:19.990 --> 03:23.700
<i>Clear condition update: 
survive for five minutes.</i>

03:24.090 --> 03:26.930
Clear Condition
 <b>Survive for five minutes</b>

03:24.510 --> 03:26.020
An endurance battle, huh?

03:27.380 --> 03:29.690
Five minutes is really all I need?

03:29.690 --> 03:31.190
So if I just stay in motion—

03:36.620 --> 03:39.280
<i>Was that attack even telegraphed?</i>

03:45.990 --> 03:48.570
I'm a fan of your confidence, kid,

03:48.570 --> 03:51.320
but I'd like to see you back it up.

03:56.500 --> 03:59.460
I get it! This might be a long five minutes!

04:00.230 --> 04:03.340
Practical Training  Opponent 10
Aberrant Woodmage
Level <b>120</b>

04:33.500 --> 04:35.210
<i>The hell is this thing made of?!</i>

04:40.910 --> 04:43.420
<i>Physical attacks won't work on it?!</i>

04:47.190 --> 04:49.930
<i>Guess I've just gotta dodge my ass off!</i>

04:55.060 --> 04:56.770
One minute has passed!

04:56.770 --> 04:59.440
You have four remaining, Sunraku-san!

04:59.680 --> 05:03.190
Now, show me every last bit

05:03.540 --> 05:05.980
of your vorpal soul.

05:11.650 --> 05:13.200
Aberrant Woodmage.

05:14.250 --> 05:16.420
<i>To put it lightly...</i>

05:18.330 --> 05:20.460
<i>This guy's a beast!</i>

05:21.090 --> 05:24.490
<i>Root-spear attacks that 
are barely telegraphed...</i>

05:33.820 --> 05:37.370
<i>Chains that look like they'll 
debuff you on contact...</i>

05:43.550 --> 05:46.470
<i>Both chase me around like it's 
their natural right to catch me,</i>

05:46.470 --> 05:49.020
<i>which really does a number 
on my will to keep dodging.</i>

06:06.600 --> 06:09.810
<i>But the worst part of all...</i>

06:17.150 --> 06:20.650
<i>is these magic attacks he slips 
in there every now and then!</i>

06:21.160 --> 06:22.060
<i>Not to mention...</i>

06:32.450 --> 06:36.660
<i>that the more time passes, 
the more he mixes up the magic types!</i>

06:39.380 --> 06:42.790
<i>Is the battle programmed so 
the attacks get denser, too?!</i>

06:45.300 --> 06:47.130
<i>The number of chains and roots increases,</i>

06:47.130 --> 06:49.600
<i>and the magic attacks start 
covering a wider area.</i>

07:05.870 --> 07:08.890
<i>If the density of the 
attacks keeps increasing...</i>

07:10.640 --> 07:13.950
<i>I'm gonna be dead before 
I ever reach five minutes!</i>

07:19.290 --> 07:21.670
<i>Another new spell for his arsenal?!</i>

07:27.970 --> 07:29.480
<i>The hell is this thing?</i>

07:30.050 --> 07:33.050
<i>He nullifies physical attacks and 
constantly adds attacks of his own?!</i>

07:33.540 --> 07:37.360
<i>I think I'd stand a better 
chance against Lycagon!</i>

07:46.810 --> 07:49.040
<i>Talk about hell for a first-time encounter.</i>

07:50.110 --> 07:51.780
<i>This is hopeless.</i>

07:53.690 --> 07:57.240
<i>I can barely think. I'm so tired.</i>

07:57.920 --> 08:01.750
<i>I'm gonna get some carbs in me, 
think up a strat and try again.</i>

08:02.330 --> 08:05.050
<i>It's not like I'm penalized 
if I die or anything.</i>

08:06.910 --> 08:08.250
<i>Who cares...</i>

08:11.260 --> 08:12.590
<i>Hang on, man.</i>

08:13.380 --> 08:15.430
<i>What's got you writing 
yourself off all of a sudden?</i>

08:17.770 --> 08:22.150
<i>Since when have you been such a pushover?</i>

08:30.340 --> 08:34.610
<i>I don't expect to go ten 
in a row on my first try.</i>

08:35.090 --> 08:36.870
<i>Nah, I'm done for.</i>

08:37.100 --> 08:38.380
<i>I'm totally screwed.</i>

08:39.230 --> 08:41.290
<i>It was the same with the Mud Digger.</i>

08:42.040 --> 08:44.960
<i>You relied on Emul. 
You gave up just like that.</i>

08:48.220 --> 08:52.430
<i>Next thing you know, 
you're cutting corners all over the place.</i>

08:53.250 --> 08:54.630
<i>What a mess.</i>

08:54.630 --> 08:58.530
<i>I think playing so many trash games 
almost turned my brain to trash, too.</i>

09:01.220 --> 09:02.790
Sunraku-san!

09:07.260 --> 09:10.560
<i>I guess it's not good to 
overdose on trashgamium.</i>

09:10.560 --> 09:13.400
<i>I've gotta even it out with some godgamium!</i>

09:19.510 --> 09:22.250
<i>Giving up when it's not 
a forced loss event...</i>

09:23.290 --> 09:26.040
<i>or cutting corners on a game that 
hasn't been broken wide open yet...</i>

09:31.090 --> 09:32.500
just doesn't make any sense!

09:35.180 --> 09:39.890
Breaking through the waves of 
attacks to reach melee range, eh?

09:40.360 --> 09:44.890
But what's the point, when all he 
can do is dish out basic strikes?

09:45.570 --> 09:47.950
I'm tired, damn it!

09:49.480 --> 09:50.520
So...

09:53.530 --> 09:56.530
I'm gonna win this thing 
and go the frick to bed!

09:58.470 --> 10:02.780
Even if you nullify physical damage, 
the attack itself still gets through, I'll bet.

10:05.480 --> 10:09.250
That's a pretty fancy staff for 
a monster to be carrying around.

10:09.250 --> 10:12.120
I wonder what'll happen if 
you've gotta do without it!

10:12.740 --> 10:17.390
Looks to me like you can't cast without it!

10:21.330 --> 10:23.490
In a post-apocalyptic world, 
you survive by looting!

10:24.850 --> 10:28.080
The shakedown skills I 
learned in <i>Unite Rounds</i>

10:28.640 --> 10:29.480
are not to be trifled with!

10:30.850 --> 10:33.030
Those are some sticky fingers 
you've got there, kid.

10:33.030 --> 10:35.980
But you've got two minutes left.

10:36.460 --> 10:39.280
I don't think you want 
to be breathing easy yet.

10:39.280 --> 10:42.410
Now, show me what you can do.

10:46.250 --> 10:49.040
Losing the staff is your 
berserk button, huh?!

10:49.040 --> 10:51.880
That's too many damn attacks!

10:51.880 --> 10:52.880
You're kidding me!

10:52.880 --> 10:54.540
A tantrum like this over one little staff?!

10:54.540 --> 10:57.550
Give a little warning before 
you go off like this, damn it!

11:04.390 --> 11:06.520
Sunraku-san, you're so close!

11:06.520 --> 11:08.130
Only one minute remains!

11:08.130 --> 11:11.450
Dodge, evade, withdraw, and run!

11:16.610 --> 11:18.540
<i>My mobility build is built for this!</i>

11:18.540 --> 11:20.740
<i>I'm not gonna just die 
after getting this close!</i>

11:23.050 --> 11:24.410
A wall?

11:26.350 --> 11:27.610
Not good!

11:28.080 --> 11:34.330
<i>Sunraku</i>

11:28.080 --> 11:34.330
<b>Drain          Exhaustion         Speed↓</b>

11:28.570 --> 11:31.060
Figured those chains would 
be debuff generators.

11:31.060 --> 11:34.960
And they've got enough punch 
to override Lycagon's Mark...

11:34.960 --> 11:38.170
<i>I won't be able to dodge like this.</i>

11:38.170 --> 11:40.480
Give it back!

11:40.920 --> 11:43.120
You want it back that badly...

11:43.120 --> 11:45.390
Then go get it, asshole!

11:59.060 --> 12:01.690
Dude, did you <i>actually</i> go fetch it?

12:02.450 --> 12:04.170
You're such a dumbass.

12:04.170 --> 12:05.950
You didn't need the silly staff.

12:05.950 --> 12:09.200
You'd have won if you'd kept 
the roots and chains coming.

12:11.420 --> 12:14.830
What a blockhead. A <i>wood</i>block head, even.

12:18.490 --> 12:19.140
Eh?

12:22.590 --> 12:25.210
Hang on a minute! I survived five minutes!

12:25.210 --> 12:26.990
Isn't it over?!

12:27.720 --> 12:31.220
Well, the five minutes was my idea, not his.

12:31.680 --> 12:34.480
It's right on the line, 
but I guess I'll pass you!

12:44.440 --> 12:46.450
You certainly showed me

12:46.940 --> 12:49.950
your vorpal soul, in spades.

12:50.970 --> 12:53.850
Huh? I thought he nullified physical attacks?

12:54.710 --> 12:56.470
You've done it!

12:56.470 --> 12:59.460
I simply <i>knew</i> you would, Sunraku-san!

13:01.420 --> 13:04.470
That's only when he's holding the staff.

13:04.470 --> 13:07.710
Without the staff he's just an animated tree.

13:07.710 --> 13:11.460
Well, that explains why 
he wanted it back so bad!

13:11.460 --> 13:14.810
And... hey, does that mean I beat the quest?!

13:14.810 --> 13:15.650
Sure does.

13:16.010 --> 13:17.550
And you'll get your reward.

13:17.550 --> 13:19.610
Finally!

13:19.840 --> 13:23.790
I hearby declare you an Honorary Rabituzan.

13:23.630 --> 13:25.990
Title

13:23.630 --> 13:25.990
<b>Honorary Rabituzan</b>

13:23.630 --> 13:25.990
acquired.

13:25.990 --> 13:29.350
Simply spectacular, Sunraku-san!

13:29.350 --> 13:31.180
Yay! Yay!

13:31.180 --> 13:33.880
Well... that's nice and all...

13:33.880 --> 13:36.000
But doesn't it come with 
a rare item or something?

13:36.260 --> 13:37.450
Oh, that's right.

13:37.450 --> 13:38.930
I almost forgot.

13:42.170 --> 13:46.550
<b>Vorpal Soul Collar
</b>lost.

13:42.170 --> 13:46.550
Accessory

13:42.190 --> 13:44.110
I'm sure you won't need that anymore.

13:44.570 --> 13:46.550
Well, be seeing you again soon.

13:46.930 --> 13:51.300
Unique Scenario

13:46.930 --> 13:51.300
<b>Invitation From Rabituza</b>

13:46.930 --> 13:51.300
cleared.

13:47.650 --> 13:51.300
<i>Unique scenario, Invitation 
From Rabituza, cleared.</i>

13:51.530 --> 13:52.290
W-Wait!

13:52.290 --> 13:53.770
I don't get to keep it?!

13:54.700 --> 13:59.580
Bonus Unique Scenario
<b>Vorpal Epic
</b>Begin now?
No  Yes

13:54.760 --> 13:59.580
<i>Bonus unique scenario, 
Vorpal Epic. Begin now?</i>

14:01.380 --> 14:03.940
Not a single piece of real loot?!

14:12.700 --> 14:16.820
Sheesh, it's the middle of the night.

14:29.850 --> 14:32.410
"When the souls of the Divinity tremble,

14:32.410 --> 14:35.530
a rabbit shall tell an epic tale"... huh?

14:35.930 --> 14:38.480
Yeah, I'm not following a word of that.

14:38.480 --> 14:52.490
Bonus Unique Scenario
<b>Vorpal Epic
</b><b>When the souls of the Divinity are shaken,
a rabbit shall tell an epic tale.
Rec. Level: <b>80</b></b>

14:38.910 --> 14:44.050
The bonus unique scenario I 
just spawned, "Vorpal Epic"...

14:44.730 --> 14:47.120
I hit "yes" to accept the quest,

14:47.120 --> 14:49.650
but I don't know how to kick it off.

14:49.650 --> 14:52.490
Plus, the recommended level is 80...

14:52.640 --> 15:00.250
Level 31

14:52.940 --> 14:54.440
"Divinity"...

14:54.780 --> 14:56.730
I think that was on the guide site.

14:56.730 --> 15:00.250
It's that civilization that died 
out a long time ago, right?

15:01.050 --> 15:04.160
All the lore and speculation got 
pretty overwhelming, though,

15:04.160 --> 15:05.750
so I backed out of that pretty quick.

15:06.380 --> 15:10.760
Pulling usable info from 
that mess won't be easy.

15:11.210 --> 15:13.990
There're whole clans dedicated 
to finding out the game lore,

15:13.990 --> 15:16.770
so no wonder there's a ton 
of stuff to sift through.

15:17.370 --> 15:19.660
Maybe I'll put the unique 
stuff on hold for now,

15:19.660 --> 15:23.030
check out the town and then 
head for the next area.

15:23.030 --> 15:24.520
Are we venturing forth?!

15:24.840 --> 15:25.840
Yep.

15:25.840 --> 15:28.030
Wait, that's right...

15:30.260 --> 15:32.340
If I head out looking like this,

15:32.340 --> 15:35.950
I'm gonna be mobbed by PKers 
and info hunters again.

15:36.530 --> 15:38.810
Even if I change my headgear,

15:38.810 --> 15:41.790
Lycagon's Mark is gonna draw attention.

15:42.120 --> 15:46.130
Not being able to wear torso and leg 
armor is screwing me over so hard!

15:46.130 --> 15:47.880
That lousy mutt!

15:48.200 --> 15:50.880
Then why not hide your entire form?

15:50.880 --> 15:53.350
That's what I'm trying 
to figure out how to do.

15:53.350 --> 15:56.140
I know just the place to get what you need!

16:00.640 --> 16:03.900
Eh? Izzat you, Emul-neechan?

16:01.160 --> 16:03.900
<b>Peatz</b>

16:04.170 --> 16:07.080
Hey, an exclusive Palace of Rabituza shop?!

16:07.080 --> 16:08.150
Sunraku-san!

16:08.150 --> 16:10.730
Allow me to introduce my 
younger brother, Peatz!

16:10.730 --> 16:14.050
He acquires goods and sells them in Rabituza!

16:14.050 --> 16:15.750
Hey, nice to meet you!

16:15.750 --> 16:17.270
Not just Rabituza.

16:17.270 --> 16:18.910
You can find me in other towns, too.

16:19.160 --> 16:22.190
I don't go out too often, since I 
gotta turn into a human to do it.

16:22.190 --> 16:24.170
But if you happen to see me, 
come by and say hi...

16:24.500 --> 16:27.700
Mr. Birdman, darling of the Night Emperor.

16:27.700 --> 16:29.460
"Birdman"?

16:29.460 --> 16:31.380
I'll have you know this is a mask,

16:31.380 --> 16:33.590
and there's a real human face underneath it!

16:33.590 --> 16:34.290
See?

16:37.180 --> 16:38.830
What's with the big show of surprise?

16:37.700 --> 16:44.440
<b>Staring Bird Mask
</b>equipped

16:38.830 --> 16:41.190
Y-You actually took it off!

16:41.190 --> 16:44.440
I had assumed there was some 
deeper reason you couldn't!

16:44.440 --> 16:45.890
Of course I can.

16:45.890 --> 16:48.440
But that's even more convenient!

16:48.440 --> 16:52.270
Peatz, did you not recently acquire 
that very intriguing textile?

16:52.270 --> 16:53.450
Say, yeah.

16:54.950 --> 16:57.590
It's a pretty neat thing so I 
figured it'd put it up for sale,

16:57.590 --> 17:00.830
but it looks pretty mundane 
relative to the price tag,

17:00.830 --> 17:03.100
so it's been hard to find a buyer.

17:03.500 --> 17:04.830
Textile?

17:06.620 --> 17:07.830
Er...

17:07.830 --> 17:11.760
A map of the area around Thirdrema. 
Is that all?

17:12.270 --> 17:14.550
Yes, that's all.

17:13.800 --> 17:15.260
<i>Sunraku</i>

17:15.620 --> 17:17.760
Thank you for coming.

17:21.770 --> 17:23.890
Actually, I've got <i>way</i> more to say!

17:24.170 --> 17:25.530
The hell is with this gear?!

17:25.530 --> 17:28.400
I'll admit it covers 
Lycagon's Mark, but still!

17:28.400 --> 17:30.640
This is a total meme costume!

17:30.640 --> 17:33.910
Sunraku-san, shouting like 
that will attract attention!

17:33.910 --> 17:36.040
I already stick out like a sore thumb!

17:36.550 --> 17:37.910
<b>Ritual Medjed Keffiyeh</b>

17:38.270 --> 17:40.450
Just endure it until we leave town!

17:40.450 --> 17:42.300
I'm sure it will all work out!

17:42.300 --> 17:44.540
Yeah, I guess it's fine.

17:44.540 --> 17:48.050
I got the recovery items 
and map I needed anyway.

17:49.080 --> 17:53.550
But boy, you burn through MP fast 
when you're in human form, huh?

17:53.960 --> 17:57.800
Let's get moving to the next 
area before our items run out.

17:59.410 --> 18:04.930
Prismatic Forest Grotto

17:59.940 --> 18:03.890
Looks like there're three places 
we can go from Thirdrema.

18:03.890 --> 18:04.930
Right-o!

18:04.930 --> 18:17.950
Prismatic Forest Grotto

18:05.200 --> 18:09.600
The Prismatic Forest Grotto 
en route to Fourfolkshire.

18:09.600 --> 18:14.100
A maze of caverns overgrowing with plant life,

18:14.100 --> 18:17.950
in which flowers of all colors bloom!

18:17.950 --> 18:27.210
Fellfate Caldera

18:18.330 --> 18:21.310
The Fellfate Caldera en route to Fivelle.

18:21.900 --> 18:27.210
Water has collected in the crater of 
a long-extinct volcano to form a lake.

18:27.210 --> 18:31.780
And the Iron Ruins of the 
Divinity en route to Sixenveldt.

18:27.210 --> 18:38.220
Iron Ruins of the Divinity

18:31.780 --> 18:33.840
Ruins from the era of the Divinity,

18:33.840 --> 18:38.220
it gets its name from its 
many hovering iron boards!

18:38.720 --> 18:39.940
I see.

18:39.940 --> 18:42.460
Which area to visit first?

18:42.460 --> 18:43.520
It's like in a wargame,

18:43.520 --> 18:47.290
where you have to decide which faction 
to play, which one to exploit,

18:47.290 --> 18:49.530
and which one to suck up to.

18:49.530 --> 18:52.480
An extremely complex decision 
on the level of that.

18:52.480 --> 18:56.070
I recommend the Fellfate Caldera!

18:56.070 --> 18:57.740
Could you please be quiet, Emul?

19:01.790 --> 19:02.930
Okay, I've decided!

19:02.930 --> 19:05.870
We'll head for the 
Prismatic Forest Grotto first!

19:06.220 --> 19:08.470
Would you like to know 
my reasoning, Emul-kun?

19:09.840 --> 19:13.380
First, the area we must avoid at all costs

19:13.380 --> 19:16.680
is clearly the Iron Ruins of the Divinity.

19:17.080 --> 19:21.380
One might hear the name and be swayed by 
the promise of scientific bounties within,

19:21.380 --> 19:22.420
but that is a trap.

19:22.420 --> 19:26.020
Science means civilization. 
Yes, the wisdom of centuries!

19:23.290 --> 19:26.640
Haven't we seen that person before?

19:26.640 --> 19:28.160
So if there're guns and stuff in the ruins,

19:28.160 --> 19:31.250
I'm gonna be a pain in the ass 
to deal with at my current stats,

19:31.250 --> 19:32.350
so hard pass.

19:32.350 --> 19:34.060
Huh? Person?

21:14.960 --> 21:22.220
<b>SLF Mini</b>

21:15.690 --> 21:19.460
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

21:18.750 --> 21:22.210
<i><b>What Sunraku Saw!</b></i>

21:19.460 --> 21:21.010
Mini!

21:22.210 --> 22:28.280
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

21:44.730 --> 21:46.830
<i>Look at that fancy box.</i>

21:46.830 --> 21:49.020
<i>Is that Vash's secret stash?</i>

21:49.350 --> 21:54.000
<i>What rare treasures could the 
boss of Rabituza have to offer?</i>

21:59.000 --> 22:01.840
<i>What the heck is in there?!</i>

22:09.500 --> 22:11.010
<i>A c-carrot?</i>

22:19.290 --> 22:23.360
<i>I guess beneath all of it, 
Aniki Vash is still a rabbit.</i>

22:28.280 --> 22:35.540
<b>SLF Mini</b>

22:28.960 --> 22:32.730
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

22:32.070 --> 22:35.530
<i><b>Memory: XX Seconds</b></i>

22:32.730 --> 22:34.330
Mini!

22:35.540 --> 23:50.630
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

22:36.600 --> 22:37.790
Now, then...

22:38.210 --> 22:41.340
The newly released Great Max Tan-Tan Noodles.

22:41.900 --> 22:44.510
I'm gonna want something 
to wash it down with.

22:49.920 --> 22:50.790
Hm?

22:50.790 --> 22:53.260
But didn't I hear water 
makes spicy stuff worse?

22:58.880 --> 23:01.080
Man, I'm so thirsty.

23:07.820 --> 23:09.820
Crap. I just chugged it like always!

23:11.050 --> 23:12.700
And it's only been a minute!

23:13.460 --> 23:15.300
But I've still got two minutes to kill.

23:19.650 --> 23:23.320
Oh, right. That game's got a log-in bonus.

23:23.320 --> 23:25.250
Maybe I'll do that real quick.

23:37.870 --> 23:40.230
I forgot about it!

23:41.630 --> 23:43.070
They soaked it all up.

23:43.440 --> 23:45.670
They're basically broth-free tan-tan noodles.

23:48.960 --> 23:49.910
Guess I'll eat it.
